## Why This Is Asked

This evaluates a candidate's ability to design resilient, multi-region metrics pipelines that can withstand regional failures while maintaining data integrity and SLAs.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-region ingestion architecture with blast radius containment
- Per-tenant quotas, token-bucket throttling, and bounded local buffering
- Idempotent writes with deterministic IDs and backpressure signaling
- Circuit breakers and automated regional failover mechanisms
- Observability metrics: ingress latency, drop rate, max replay delay
- Adaptive sampling for surge handling

## Code Example

```javascript
// pseudo-code for idempotent write with backpressure
function writeWithBackpressure(metric) {
  const id = generateDeterministicId(metric);
  if (isBackpressureActive()) {
    bufferLocally(metric);
    return;
  }
  return idempotentWrite(id, metric);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to diagnose rate-limiter issues, design clear observability, and execute a controlled rollback with minimal disruption.

## Key Concepts
- Token bucket rate limiting across regions
- Observability for distributed systems
- Canary testing and safe traffic shifts
- Rollback and validation under time pressure
- Post-incident analysis and preventive fixes

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo token bucket core (simplified)
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, capacity) { this.rate = rate; this.capacity = capacity; this.tokens = capacity; this.last = Date.now(); }
  allow() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const delta = (now - this.last) * this.rate / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + delta);
    this.last = now;
    if (this.tokens >= 1) { this.tokens -= 1; return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```
